# Example cron schedule for this project (macOS/Linux).
#
# Install with: crontab -e   (paste the lines below, adjusting PROJECT_DIR
# and VENV_PYTHON to your actual paths), or:
#   (crontab -l 2>/dev/null; cat crontab.example) | crontab -
#
# Adjust PROJECT_DIR to wherever you unzipped/cloned this project, and
# VENV_PYTHON to your virtualenv's python (e.g. PROJECT_DIR/.venv/bin/python).

PROJECT_DIR=/absolute/path/to/howsmytrain
VENV_PYTHON=/absolute/path/to/howsmytrain/.venv/bin/python

# Poll every 2 hours between 5am and 11pm IST (10 runs/day) -- each run polls
# EVERY train number in TRAIN_NUMBERS, so total daily requests = (cron runs
# per day) x (number of trains tracked). RailRadar's free tier caps at 50
# requests/day, 10/min burst, so budget accordingly:
#   - 1-2 trains  -> every 1 hour is safe (~18-36 req/day)
#   - 3-4 trains  -> every 2 hours is safe (~40-60 req/day, watch the top end)
#   - 5+ trains   -> every 3-4 hours, or narrow the cron hour range to each
#                    train's actual running window instead of 5am-11pm
0 5-23/2 * * * cd $PROJECT_DIR && $VENV_PYTHON scripts/poll_once.py >> logs/poll.log 2>&1

# Generate the weekly markdown report every Monday at 8am IST.
0 8 * * 1 cd $PROJECT_DIR && $VENV_PYTHON scripts/weekly_report.py >> logs/weekly_report.log 2>&1
